,"position":{"commit_sha":"227ea7eeb61a5002736040f32ef8176312e69776","position":"1786447054480536001-5b46ceaa-34fd-4682-99f4-e151cb735685"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"823f87f3c6fb7ea0a3fe7d90a200d613e9e63ce3f4f5076eae219a878a3930af","event_uuid":"0711e00d-b55f-4c73-984a-57f7395ba17b","position":{"commit_sha":"8abbfa7ab9c90644cd786cbfed55f4ba2b45d787","position":"1786447058597145001-0711e00d-b55f-4c73-984a-57f7395ba17b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"SPLIT (2026-08-07). This ticket was too large and its plan review never converged: four rounds\nproduced 2 -> 7 -> 4 -> 7 blocking findings. The pattern was structural, not editorial — every verb\nthe ticket touched dragged its own unenumerated consumer set (workflows, pressure-test scripts,\ncanary wiring, contract tests, docs), so remediating one verb's findings surfaced the next verb's.\nSplitting it makes each consumer set reviewable on its own.\n\nThis ticket is RESCOPED to the surface itself — registering the `bridge` noun and its subcommand\ndispatch, plus the two verbs with no predecessor to rename from (`preview`, `sync`). It keeps: the\nscoped functional ACs (preview performs no Jira write and no ticket-event write; sync mutates), the\nB1 note that pause/resume/status behavioural assertions belong to `1104-93eb-6ce0-4a19` /\n`b69c-5787-81b8-4052` because an edge back would be a cycle, the B4 decision that `mode.py`'s\nMODE_CAPS and Mode ladder SURVIVE, and the corrected doctor AC (the bridge health verb is\n`bridge fsck`; the EXISTING top-level `rebar doctor` store link-repair command at\n`_cli/__init__.py:323` is preserved, with a test asserting it still dispatches).\n\nThe six existing `depends_on` edges into this ticket (`1104`, `424f`, `030f`, `b69c`, `9895`,\n`f789`) are unchanged and remain correct — they attach their verbs to the surface this ticket\ncreates.\n\nCarved out:\n\n* `c61a-9f8f-8ef9-4601` — \"Retire the two dead bridge verbs (bridge-status, purge-bridge)\".\n  Pure dead-code deletion, NO dependency on any sibling; can land immediately. Carries the B6\n  user-facing-string cleanup (`_engine_support/bridge.py:32`'s `_USAGE`,\n  `schemas/bridge_status.schema.json`) and the dangling \"epic 3a03\" citation, which dies with the\n  module.\n* `4a44-4abb-ae91-4e51` — \"Retire the reconcile verb and the --mode flag (CLI + engine)\".\n  `depends_on` this ticket. Carries B3 (the `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml:262`\n  epic-3006 rollback-brake migration + the same-change `workflow_dispatch` input rename, with the\n  full mode -> new-surface mapping), B2 (the four direct engine callers in\n  `scripts/jira-pressure-test/`), B5 (`--filter-local-ids` -> `--only` in those same scripts), the\n  B3 test-consumer MIGRATION list, and the surface-scope note that the library\n  `rebar.reconcile(mode=)` and the MCP `reconcile` tool are retired by `f789`, not here.\n* `e27c-5a20-cd13-43b2` — \"Rename the three surviving bridge verbs onto the bridge noun\"\n  (`bridge-fsck` -> `bridge fsck`, `bridge-probe` -> `bridge check-access`, `jira-onboard` ->\n  `bridge setup`). `depends_on` this ticket. States explicitly that `check-access` and `setup` are\n  RENAMES of shipping code, not new features — which is what the reviews kept catching — and\n  enumerates each verb's consumer set (freshly grepped, including the string-named sites a symbol\n  search misses). Keeps the decision that `setup` calls `check-access` as its final validation step\n  and the rationale for `check-access` being its own verb (all three narrowing-flag precedents are\n  read-only; this creates and deletes a real Jira issue).\n\nNew edges: `4a44` depends_on this; `e27c` depends_on this; `030f-c14f-596a-4f79` depends_on `e27c`\n(030f edits bridge_fsck, which e27c renames); `f789-3f9d-8b35-4e0d` depends_on `4a44` (f789 retires\nthe library/MCP reconcile that 4a44 retires on the CLI). `c61a` has no edges by design.","timestamp":1786095805955605001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Child b42a-ffc3-deeb-4491 is closed after its completion verifier passed all ten criteria against 43448cd486. Its implementation landed as Gerrit 1527 / origin/main 45ad7d3ece with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments, and successful full CI run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31229199537. Compatibility follow-ups Gerrit 1530 and 1531 are also merged and green, pinning five-mode rank/cap behavior and the real reconcile-check ref round trip without removing any legacy command, workflow vocabulary, or environment contract.","timestamp":1786157643020759001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion-verifier documentation evidence at merged ref 43448cd486: docs/user-guide.md:379-384 documents only bridge preview and bridge sync while explicitly preserving reconcile, jira-onboard, bridge-probe, bridge-fsck, and doctor; docs/cli-reference.md:25-35 generates the bridge group with exactly preview and sync; docs/release-notes.md:10-16 states these are the only bridge-group verbs and lists the preserved legacy workflows. No unimplemented sibling verb is advertised in those staged-surface sections.","timestamp":1786158084274524001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Observed 2026-08-07 in /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-bridge-2f79 at ref 43448cd486: child b42a-ffc3-deeb-4491 completion verification returned PASS for all ten acceptance criteria, including its held-out preview no-write oracle, sync persisted-mutation oracle, legacy-command continuity, generated docs, and external gate criterion; the child then transitioned closed. Its code landed as Gerrit 1527 / commit 45ad7d3ece with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments, and successful full matrix https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31229199537. Focused 103 tests, make lint, and make typecheck passed before push; the cited CI run supplied the full make-test-equivalent evidence.","timestamp":1786158088360141001}],"created_at":1786047482259664001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\nEstablish the provider-neutral `bridge` noun through a safe, working vertical slice. This story is the dependency root for later verb migrations, so it must land without breaking any workflow, environment, script, library caller, or user that still relies on the old vocabulary.\n\nThe earlier plan advertised all eight final verbs before their owning stories implemented them. That would ship broken placeholders on `main`. The corrected staged contract is:\n\n- this story ships only functional `bridge preview` and `bridge sync`;\n- the legacy top-level `reconcile`, `jira-onboard`, `bridge-probe`, and `bridge-fsck` commands remain fully functional;\n- downstream stories add `setup`, `check-access`, `fsck`, `status`, `pause`, and `resume` only together with their real handlers and consumer migrations;\n- no placeholder or not-implemented verb is advertised.\n\nThe final epic surface remains `setup | check-access | fsck | status | preview | sync | pause | resume`. Top-level `rebar doctor` is unrelated store link repair and remains untouched; no `bridge doctor` spelling ships.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- `preview` forces the existing dry-run engine path and performs no Jira or ticket-store mutation.\n- `sync` forces the existing live engine path and mutates.\n- Callers cannot pass `--mode` or `--filter-local-ids` through this foundation and override the read/write distinction.\n- Public `--max-changes`, `--only`, and `--except` remain owned by story `4a44-4abb-ae91-4e51`, which makes preview/sync primary and migrates their consumers in one continuity-preserving change. `--max-age` belongs to `bridge status` and remains owned by status story `b69c-5787-81b8-4052`, whose canonical and legacy status routes share that option.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mode.py` survives. `MODE_CAPS` and the `Mode` rank ladder remain required by the MCP surface and the phase-gate compatibility value `gated_mode: \"reconcile-check\"`.\n- Library/MCP parity belongs to `f789-3f9d-8b35-4e0d`; workflow/script migration belongs to `4a44-4abb-ae91-4e51`.\n\n## Decomposition\n\nChild `b42a-ffc3-deeb-4491` owns the complete vertical slice: nested dispatch, working preview/sync behavior, help, docs, real CLI oracle, and compatibility coverage. It is intentionally one child rather than an architectural-layer split because the interface must ship with its first consumers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `rebar bridge preview` is functional and read-only; `rebar bridge sync` is functional and mutating.\n- [x] Group/no-verb/help/unknown-verb behavior is explicit, and nested names never fall through to top-level commands.\n- [x] No sibling-owned verb is advertised before its functional implementation lands.\n- [x] Every legacy command and every current in-repo consumer keeps working at this story boundary.\n- [x] `Mode`, `MODE_CAPS`, and the real `gated_mode: \"reconcile-check\"` round trip remain intact.\n- [x] Top-level `rebar doctor` remains functional and `bridge doctor` remains unknown.\n- [x] User guide, generated CLI reference, and release notes describe only the staged surface that actually ships.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Child `b42a-ffc3-deeb-4491` passes its held-out behavioral oracle and all project gates.\n\n## Rollback\n\nThe surface is additive and changes no persisted schema. Revert the child's Gerrit change to remove the nested group while leaving all legacy vocabulary and consumers intact.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"new nested group and working preview/sync vertical slice"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"route bridge noun while preserving all legacy command wrappers"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge.txt","reason":"help for only functional staged verbs"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt","reason":"advertise bridge noun"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli.py","reason":"real CLI read/write and compatibility oracle"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","reason":"new help-backed noun coverage"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"document staged bridge surface"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"regenerated nested CLI reference"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"additive surface release note without premature retirement claims"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1786442617031042479,"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f79-2b32-28c5-4eb3","parent_status_uuid":"5b46ceaa-34fd-4682-99f4-e151cb735685","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["bridge","ux"],"ticket_id":"4752-3afb-e8bd-448a","ticket_type":"story","title":"Establish the bridge verb group (noun + subcommand dispatch)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1bb33bc5-e04a-4dfd-9e9a-09dc006002e6","d28c5f9d-1f3b-4aa6-a499-4917577b32ce","b121e240-c912-4caa-bc64-269bf4e8b9fa","b2153bb1-f15a-4a7a-8315-4f019b82f359","fdc07415-267b-49ae-ac1b-5430dd6baf81","9b2426b1-9bdc-4763-9825-8b62702149fe","040f2136-1be9-4fa7-9458-b8e5da610ae2","8fac7cea-c979-496f-8c9c-769248654417","73367356-7f42-40e7-9569-6b6b73ce7c0e","9818b0ef-87e0-4cbd-a1f7-74535ed82924","adc03b63-4b2f-4b5d-a44a-3f97b25909ee","ddaa04d1-1b1b-4408-abde-2ba4ff9e06b4","0e88a263-4c59-475f-95dd-ceb566f67f3c","585ad828-b09c-4be1-ab4d-6f28dee7edcd","efdd525a-cb2f-464a-b4e5-3c18d156b2b8","85736f19-57cc-4da4-a81d-1d40ce8fa5fc","33bfcb82-828c-4223-b06e-52ca2c6b6459","f50b7003-0e52-4a9b-9e3f-b2c91c7f47a8","5b46ceaa-34fd-4682-99f4-e151cb735685","0711e00d-b55f-4c73-984a-57f7395ba17b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659564995932001,"uuid":"62b9e296-d42f-4798-b195-9bbd357a7878"}